recentTrajectories.summary:
Problem

  Current getMyConversations() in chat.service.ts (lines 80-122) executes:
  1. One query to fetch all conversations
  2. N separate queries — one prisma.message.count() per conversation to get unread count

  For a user with 50 conversations: 51 database queries instead of 2.

  Current Code (lines 106-119)

  // Add unread count for each conversation
  const withUnread = await Promise.all(
    conversations.map(async (conv) => {
      const unreadCount = await prisma.message.count({
        where: {
          conversationId: conv.id,
          receiverId: userId,
          isRead: false,
          isDeleted: false,
        },
      });
      return { ...conv, unreadCount };
    }),
  );

  Solution

  Replace the per-conversation count with a single grouped query using prisma.message.groupBy:

  // Single query to get unread counts for all conversations
  const unreadCounts = await prisma.message.groupBy({
    by: ['conversationId'],
    where: {
      receiverId: userId,
      isRead: false,
      isDeleted: false,
      conversationId: { in: conversations.map(c => c.id) }, // filter only relevant convos
    },
    _count: { id: true },
  });

  // Convert to Map for O(1) lookup
  const unreadMap = new Map(unreadCounts.map(r => [r.conversationId, r._count.id]));

  // Attach counts without additional queries
  const withUnread = conversations.map(conv => ({
    ...conv,
    unreadCount: unreadMap.get(conv.id) || 0,
  }));

  Implementation Steps

  1. Read chat.service.ts — you already have the full context
  2. Modify getMyConversations() — after fetching conversations, add the grouped query above, then map results
  3. Keep the existing conversation fetch — that stays as-is (lines 81-104)
  4. TypeScript — the groupBy result needs type annotation, use as { conversationId: string; _count: { id: number } }[] or explicit typing
  5. Run typecheck — npm run typecheck --workspace=@lancr/server

  Verification

  - Before: 51 queries for 50 conversations
  - After: 2 queries (conversation fetch + groupBy) — regardless of conversation count
